# TODO - Jig repository governance

## Objective

Integrate the evolving Jig validator through the system `PATH`, preserve its
fail-closed rules, and configure only genuine project-specific differences
without weakening unrelated linter contracts.

## Acceptance

- The Jig installation selected from `PATH`, `.jig/jig.toml` bootstrap, and
  `.jig/settings/` generation describe the actual polyglot repository without
  fake language/tool requirements or weakened reviewed lint policy.
- The authoritative rule/specification is deterministic, versionable, and does
  not depend on undocumented host behavior.
- The declared scope contains no unresolved placeholder implementation or
  undocumented workaround required for this objective to function.
- Evidence is durable enough to move this TODO to `docs/todo/completed/` and
  remove the exact TODO heading without losing unfinished intent.

## Evidence

- Jig 26.3.0 is resolved through the system `PATH`; repository-local launchers
  are not part of the validation boundary.
- `.jig/jig.toml` schema 21 pins the modular schema-1 `.jig/settings/`
  generation. Those settings declare the typed TODO workflow, lifecycle roots,
  exact sections, acceptance evidence, validation commands, strict dependency
  lanes, and closed change-class path policy.
- `.jig/settings/repository.toml` explicitly disables source-mirrored tests
  because root `tests/` is accepted repository-wide evidence.
- Git governance additionally declares `JIG_SHIT.md` as a required
  local-only QA ledger. The tracked root `.gitignore` owns `/JIG_SHIT.md`, so
  agents may record Jig integration defects without accidentally promoting that
  scratch evidence into repository history.
- The installed commit-message hook resolves `jig` through `PATH`, parses the
  schema-21 modular configuration, and accepts new compliant commits
  fail-closed.
- `tests/test_governance_paths.py` rejects duplicated nested `.jig` path
  segments in authored text outside the validator-owned configuration tree.
- `jig validate --root .` is the canonical command and invokes the installed,
  versioned validator without a repository-local Jig checkout.
- Historical repair plan
  `5f7e10afc710f9c47093d68f853d26657f8854aa` normalized 32 messages across
  208 linear unsigned commits while preserving every tree, identity, timestamp,
  and chronological position. The original tip remains under the Jig backup ref.
- The repaired history has zero `JIG-COMMIT-*` diagnostics, and complete
  schema-21 validation is the current repository closure gate.
- Prerequisite completion evidence: `repository-responsibility-scaffold`.
- **Completion:** Completed on 2026-08-06 after initial repository governance,
  typed TODO policy, repaired historical messages, governance-path tests, and
  full Jig validation passed with zero diagnostics. The integration was later
  migrated to schema 21, modular settings, and the system `PATH` authority.
